    <mj-wrapper background-color="#006837" padding="0">
    <!-- The 16px inset is SPACER RAILS, not section padding, and must stay that
         way: this is a background-url section, so it compiles inside a v:rect,
         and Outlook cannot honor horizontal padding there (guide §4). It was
         briefly converted to padding="32px 64px" on 2026-08-22 to put the
         gutter somewhere the mobile rule could reach; that traded an Outlook
         defect for a mobile one, and is reverted. The rails carry a width pin
         instead — the same idiom .poll-icon and .stream-icon use, and the only
         thing that reaches a group child on a phone, because a group converts
         px widths to inline percentages below the breakpoint (unpinned, the
         earlier 64px cut's rail measured 40px at 375; today's 16px rail would
         drift the same way, even though its desktop width now equals the pin). -->
      <mj-section css-class="image-block block" background-url="assets/photo-forest.jpg" background-size="cover" background-repeat="no-repeat" background-position="center center" padding="32px 0 32px">
